    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420">

                <pb facs="0520" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/4–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Benninghoff</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dairen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-07">April [7?],
                        1947</date>.<lb/>[Received April 13—8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>57. Advance information is requested concerning any American participation in
                    proposed Chinese expedition from Tsingtao.</p>
                <p>Can we expect US Navy, diplomatic courier, or correspondents? <pb facs="0521"
                        n="511" xml:id="pg511"/> Also would appreciate instructions if any which
                    Dept or Embassy may have, especially reference last parts mytel 55.<anchor
                        n="65" xml:id="d420-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 57; in reply to Nanking’s 8, April 2;<anchor n="66" xml:id="d420-f2"
                    /> see mytel 55, April 5.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Benninghoff</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
